"""Compositional ovstage population helpers for the physics domain.

A prim is a type plus applied API schemas. Build a batch of prims sharing one
type and one API set, then write it in a single upsert::

    batch = PrimBatch(paths, ['/World/Box_0', '/World/Box_1'])
    batch.define_cube(size=[50.0, 50.0], local_matrix=matrices)
    batch.apply_physics_rigid_body_api()
    batch.apply_physics_collision_api()
    batch.write(stage, ordinal=1)

Per-prim values are Python sequences or CPU ``warp`` arrays: shape ``(N,)`` for
scalar columns and ``(N, lanes)`` for vector, quaternion and matrix columns.
Every ancestor of a physics prim needs a row too (the consumer composes world
transforms up the chain): use ``ancestor_paths()`` and ``define_xform()`` for them.
Omitted columns take the parser default documented in the contract; producers that
want to mirror USD population column-for-column use ``resolved_defaults()``.

This module imports ``warp`` and ``ovstage`` on first use only. It does not touch
PhysX: verification of what these columns produce lives in the generated C++
contract tests, which read the PhysX objects back through the C API.
"""

